TQMesh by Florian Setzwein, a header-only two-dimensional mesh generator for triangular and
quadrilateral elements, is used by pyoomph but is NOT part of this repository: it is downloaded at
build time by cmake/ThirdPartyTQMesh.cmake, which pins the exact revision, and prepared by
citools/patches/patch_tqmesh.cmake. It is compiled into the extension module, i.e. it is contained
in the python wheels, which is why its licence is reproduced below.

TQMesh is hosted at https://github.com/FloSewn/TQMesh

pyoomph exposes it to python in src/nanobind/tqmesh/, and pyoomph/meshes/tqmesh.py builds on that
with the TQMeshTemplate. Both are dropped from the build - and the download skipped - by
-DPYOOMPH_HAS_TQMESH=OFF.

